- "Personal Use" means use by a single individual on hardware they own
  or control, for non-commercial learning, research, note-taking, and
  personal automation, without redistribution to third parties.
- "Commercial Use" means use by an entity for revenue, internal
  business operations, employee productivity at scale, or any
  redistribution that competes with the Licensee's hosted offering.
- "Fork" means a copy of the Work whose primary branch points at the
  Licensee's repository and that preserves this license file verbatim.
- "Contribution" means any patch, pull request, skill body, source
  adapter, or documentation change submitted back to the Licensee
  through the upstream repository.
- "Derivative Work" means any work that builds on, embeds, links
  against, or depends on the Work in a way that requires its presence
